  "body": "The Machines pane's file editor gets an \"Axis chain\" group. The group adds, moves and removes the axis parts of a `.mch` file, reverses a linear axis, and sets the direction of a rotary axis. The editor changes the file's own JSON, so it keeps every key that it does not know. The decisions and the open questions are in `docs/decisions/2756-machine-axis-chain.md`.\n\n![The Axis chain group on a 3-axis mill, above General](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roer70/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2756/axis-chain.png)\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`MachineDraft`** (`crates/app/src/machine/chain.rs`, `draft.rs`) adds, moves and removes axis parts in `kinematics.default.parts`, like `add_coolant` and `remove_coolant`. A refused edit changes nothing. The validator judges the result as before.\n  - A new axis goes **on the table** (beside the table's axes, before the head; a rotary there turns the work) or **carries the head** (it takes the head's slot; a rotary there tilts the tool).\n  - **Remove** keeps what the axis carried: its `parts` take its place, in order. Its controller row goes with it.\n  - **Up and Down** trade an axis with its neighbour row. The tree keeps its shape, so a move never changes which slot carries the head. An axis keeps all its own keys (`pivot`, `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, `sign_convention`, unknown keys) and gets the `parent` and `chain_order` (#1962) of its new slot.\n  - A move trades only with an axis of the same kind (rotary or linear) that moves the same thing (the work or the tool). Other moves are refused, and the refusal says to remove the axis and add it again.\n  - A linear is reversed with `\"direction\": -1` (#373). Back to standard removes the key.\n  - A rotary's `axis` is ±X, ±Y, ±Z or three numbers. The editor suggests the RS-274 letter (about X is A, about Y is B, about Z is C) and adds a note to a row whose letter does not agree. It does not refuse it.\n- **The validator** keys the work-length refusals by axis and key (`A nose_to_axis`, `work_length_refusals` in `crates/post/src/machine/swing.rs`), so each refusal shows at its row and not above the grid. The rule is the parser's own rule.\n- **The editor rows** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/machine_axis_chain.rs`) draw in one property grid, like General and the editor's other groups (`prop_grid` in `layout/form.rs`, #1122): one setting per row, the label in the first column and the control beside it, help as a hover text. A first version pushed the controls to the right edge (`prop_row`), so in a wide pane they drifted away from their labels. Each axis has a row with its letter and kind and the buttons Up, Down and ✖. Their accessible names are \"Move A up\", \"Move A down\" and \"Remove A\". The direction and the place of a new axis are dropdowns.\n  - `nose_to_axis` (#804) and `axis_to_table` (#1107) are rows for a rotary that turns the work. A rotary that carries the head shows them only when the file states one, so that the user can clear it.\n  - A row whose `offset` has no parent rotary gets a note (see Q1 below).\n  - The fields have stable ids, so a note or a refusal that comes or goes above a field does not take the focus while the user types.\n- The Machines pane's editor and detail view fill the width of the pane.\n\nThe machine window (\"edit a machine\" from the Setup pane) also has \"add axis\". That window edits the mounted `Machine` (a flat list of axes and limits) through `EditMachineApply`. This group edits the axis tree of the `.mch` file and keeps the keys that the editor does not know. They are two different tools, and this PR does not change the machine window.\n\n## Open questions (the decision file takes the recommended option)\n\nThe maintainer has not answered these yet. Each one has a cost to change in the decision file.\n\n- **Q1** (comment of 2026-11-20): an `offset` on a rotary with no parent rotary. This PR shows a note at the row and does not refuse the file. We recommend a refusal in the validator.\n- **Q2** (comment of 2026-11-20): a move trades only with an axis of the same kind. This PR also refuses a trade between an axis that moves the work and one that moves the tool.\n- The three questions in the issue: the order with #1970, the #785 pair beside the #1962 pair, and a machine with a tilting head and a rotary table. This PR adds a head axis and a table axis to the same file, but does not draw a \"Kinematics\" group.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on `e0e4fee68`: 124 steps, 0 failed, 7.5 min.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main` on `e0e4fee68`: 4 steps, 0 failed, 5.0 min.\n- The gate's batch plan, run one step at a time, on `303188d61` (before the last merge of main): 1,073 steps. One red step was `a_kind_that_is_not_a_kind_refuses_at_the_door`, which main has since fixed (\"router\" is now a kind). The suite `machine` is green after the merge.\n- No heavy step: the issue is `P6`, not `P1` under the safety floor.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n31 new tests, none removed. The new app tests are modules of the existing `machine` suite (`crates/app/tests/machine/`), so this PR adds no test binary (#3187).\n\n- `crates/app/tests/machine/axis_chain.rs` (15): add on the table and with the head, remove, move, the refusals, unknown keys kept, and `a_rotary_that_turns_the_work_never_trades_with_one_that_tilts_the_tool`.\n- `crates/app/tests/machine/axis_rows.rs` (9): what each row says, the RS-274 letter note, the offset note, reverse, turn about, and the work lengths.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/machines_axis_chain.rs` (7): the group through AccessKit labels: an A added on the table, moved and saved; a refused letter and a remove; X reversed and set back; a turn about Y that suggests B and a note for an A about Y; the FlexiHAL router built from a blank mill and saved; the offset note; and a field that keeps its focus when a refusal goes away.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/machines_edit.rs`: `pick_kind` scrolls the dropdown into view first, because the group makes the form taller.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The offset-note UI test was written after the note, so it was not seen red first.\n- No output was posted from a machine file that this editor wrote. The values feed the clearance gates and the post kinematics through `parse_mch`, which the app tests check.\n- The \"Kinematics\" group (`pivot`, `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, `controller.rtcp` as fields) is #1970's. This PR keeps those keys on every edit and does not draw them.\n- `validate.rs`, `egui_app/mod.rs`, `egui_app/tests.rs` and `tests/machine.rs` are over 400 lines on main. This PR adds 1, 1, 1 and 9 lines to them.\n\nChangelog: The Machines file editor adds, moves and removes the axes of a machine, reverses a linear axis and sets a rotary's direction.\n\nFixes #2756\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
